  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 955 PM CDT Mon Jun 1 2026\n\nWarm and dry weather continues through Friday with an upper ridge\nremaining across the region. Highs will warm gradually warm mid\nweek through Friday, from low 80s on Wednesday to upper 80s by\nThursday and Friday. Lows will remain comfortable in the upper 50s\nto low 60s. This period will feel ideal for outdoor activities,\nwith light winds and minimal cloud cover allowing plenty of time\nto enjoy the sunshine after the recent active weather. \n\nBy late Friday into the weekend, the ridge will weaken somewhat, \nallowing moisture to gradually return. Showers and thunderstorms \nchances will increase, as more of a typical summertime pattern\nreturns through the weekend. Some storms could be strong, through\nwidespread severe weather is not currently anticipated. \n\nEarly next week, the patterns stays generally warmer than aver,\nwith highs int eh mid to upper 80s. Rain chances will fluctuate\nbut should stay on the low end.",
